"<p>The <b>subjunctive</b> isn't a tense but a <b>mood</b>: it expresses that something isn't stated as a fact but is <b>wished, recommended, doubted or felt</b>.</p>\n <table><tr><th>Indicative (fact)</th><th>Subjunctive (wish)</th></tr>\n <tr><td class=\"es-t\">Laia habla español.</td><td class=\"es-t\">Quiero que Laia hable español.</td></tr>\n <tr><td class=\"es-t\">Hace sol.</td><td class=\"es-t\">Ojalá haga sol.</td></tr></table>\n <p>Typical: <b>two different people</b> – I want <b>you</b> to …: <span class=\"es-t\">Quiero que (tú) vengas.</span></p>\n <div class=\"ex\">Same person → infinitive: <span class=\"es-t\">Quiero venir.</span> – not <s>quiero que venga</s>.</div>",
"Regular forms: swap the ending",
