"If you're coming to Barcelona for the first time, here are some tips. First of all, I recommend buying a travel card: it's much cheaper than single tickets. Don't carry your wallet in your back pocket, especially on the metro and on the Ramblas, because there are lots of pickpockets.\n\nFor food, don't go to restaurants with photos on the menu; you'd better look for a small bar in Gràcia or Poble-sec. And don't be surprised if people have dinner at ten at night. Finally, it's important to say a few words in Catalan: everyone likes a simple “bon dia” or “gràcies”. Enjoy the city!",
